WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:04.770
Shirakawa-san's boyfriend...

00:04.770 --> 00:05.980
is me!

00:10.680 --> 00:13.080
Huh? What is he talking about?

00:13.080 --> 00:14.780
There's no way, right?

00:15.180 --> 00:17.320
Did you hear what he just said?

00:18.640 --> 00:19.710
But it's true.

00:19.710 --> 00:20.750
Huh?

00:24.990 --> 00:27.290
If she is going out with a dork like Kashima,

00:27.290 --> 00:29.610
she must be a totally sweet girl!

00:29.610 --> 00:31.980
Shirakawa-san really is an angel!

00:31.980 --> 00:34.510
Damn it! I'm gonna ask her out again!

00:34.930 --> 00:39.630
Does that mean the rumors about her 
leeching off her boyfriends were all lies?

00:39.630 --> 00:40.920
Uh-huh.

00:53.240 --> 00:54.320
Hey, Kasshi!

00:58.260 --> 00:59.620
Kurose-san!

01:00.040 --> 01:01.110
Stay away.

01:01.790 --> 01:06.040
You're the one who spread those rumors 
about Shirakawa-san, aren't you?

01:06.820 --> 01:08.380
So what if I was?

01:08.380 --> 01:10.410
Will you talk to me about it?

01:10.410 --> 01:12.250
Why did you do something like that?

01:14.310 --> 01:16.540
I want to be number one.

01:16.540 --> 01:20.350
I don't want to let that tramp 
take anything else from me.

01:20.350 --> 01:21.560
Huh?

01:21.870 --> 01:25.520
Runa Shirakawa is my twin sister!

01:25.520 --> 01:26.710
Huh?!

01:39.450 --> 01:46.080
<b>Our Dating Story: 
The Experienced You and The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:58.420 --> 03:01.740
Twin? You're kidding.

03:01.740 --> 03:08.700
<b>Our Jealousy Story:</b>

03:02.180 --> 03:05.370
I know we don't look it. We're fraternal twins.

03:02.260 --> 03:08.700
<b>The Inexperienced You Gets</b>

03:02.760 --> 03:08.700
<b>Jealous of the Experienced You</b>

03:05.370 --> 03:06.700
But your last names...?

03:06.700 --> 03:11.670
In fifth grade, our parents divorced. 
I took my mom's last name.

03:12.140 --> 03:16.510
Mom remarried after that 
but got divorced again last month,

03:16.510 --> 03:18.760
so we moved back in with Grandpa.

03:19.440 --> 03:21.980
You're really Shirakawa-san's little sister?

03:21.980 --> 03:24.220
You have no idea how much I wish I wasn't.

03:24.540 --> 03:25.300
Huh?

03:27.840 --> 03:32.860
Runa was always the attention-seeker. 
She got everyone in the family to spoil her,

03:32.860 --> 03:37.860
but I kept more to myself and always 
had trouble expressing my feelings.

03:39.170 --> 03:42.600
I'm the one who had to move. 
I'm the one who had to change my name.

03:42.600 --> 03:47.120
I'm the one who had to transfer. 
<i>I'm</i> the one who always got treated unfairly!

03:47.630 --> 03:49.290
I realized back then

03:49.630 --> 03:54.040
that I'd never be happy unless 
I became a lovable girl like Runa,

03:54.810 --> 03:57.150
so I worked hard to change myself.

03:57.150 --> 04:00.390
I'd show her that I could become 
a girl that everyone loves too!

04:00.790 --> 04:01.970
But even then,

04:02.360 --> 04:05.210
she was still number one.

04:05.210 --> 04:06.430
Everyone in class...

04:06.430 --> 04:09.640
everyone in the whole school loved her!

04:09.640 --> 04:12.600
And that's why you spread those 
rumors about Shirakawa-san?

04:13.650 --> 04:15.560
You must think I'm disgusting.

04:16.930 --> 04:22.780
What you did is wrong, Kurose-san. 
But I think I understand how you feel.

04:23.130 --> 04:25.490
You don't understand a thing about me!

04:26.850 --> 04:31.170
It's true. I don't really know 
how you feel about your parents.

04:31.170 --> 04:36.080
But you're kind of like me... 
At least, I think so.

04:37.290 --> 04:41.520
I have trouble opening up 
about my feelings too,

04:41.520 --> 04:44.360
but I still worry about 
other people's opinions.

04:44.360 --> 04:47.340
Does everybody hate me? 
I always start wondering that.

04:47.860 --> 04:50.820
I think we're alike in that way.

04:52.120 --> 04:57.810
When I look at Shirakawa-san, I see someone 
so different... She always surprises me.

04:58.340 --> 05:02.650
She's honest and up-front with everyone. 
Natural and straightforward.

05:04.050 --> 05:06.910
She shines like the sun. But still,

05:07.210 --> 05:11.640
if you and I forced ourselves 
to act more like Shirakawa-san,

05:11.640 --> 05:13.580
I think it would only be painful for us.

05:14.370 --> 05:16.830
I know that already!

05:16.830 --> 05:19.350
I'm sure you'll find someone, Kurose-san.

05:21.090 --> 05:25.220
Someday, when you meet 
the person that you truly like,

05:25.800 --> 05:29.990
why don't you just aspire to be 
a person that he will love?

05:32.230 --> 05:33.560
Kurose-san?

05:34.520 --> 05:37.600
What? I-Is that supposed to cheer me up?

05:39.060 --> 05:40.950
A-Are you okay?

05:43.370 --> 05:44.990
Leave me alone.

05:46.320 --> 05:47.700
All right.

05:56.080 --> 05:57.690
This is the worst.

06:00.050 --> 06:01.210
Ryuto!

06:01.670 --> 06:03.160
Shirakawa-san.

06:05.090 --> 06:06.550
Hey, you.

06:07.540 --> 06:09.010
That was pretty rad.

06:09.010 --> 06:09.990
Huh?

06:11.410 --> 06:13.740
I've got work, so see ya.

06:15.090 --> 06:16.730
Have a good day.

06:24.500 --> 06:26.110
Are you okay with this, Ryuto?

06:26.520 --> 06:30.570
I know you really didn't want people 
to know that we're dating.

06:30.570 --> 06:37.380
Yeah, but I was getting sick of people 
having the wrong idea about you.

06:39.270 --> 06:41.000
You did it... for me?

06:43.920 --> 06:46.090
Oh, what? What's gotten into me?

06:46.500 --> 06:52.720
I'm just a dumb girl. I never thought rumors 
and stuff like that would get to me.

06:53.050 --> 06:54.680
Shirakawa-san...

06:54.680 --> 06:59.980
So, yeah. I guess you and Maria 
must have heard those rumors too.

07:00.400 --> 07:02.500
I wonder who started them.

07:03.400 --> 07:04.400
About that...

07:04.400 --> 07:07.860
Maria told you, right? About her and me?

07:07.860 --> 07:11.070
Uh, yeah. I just found out.

07:11.070 --> 07:14.660
Sorry about that. I tried to tell you sooner,

07:15.300 --> 07:17.660
but my timing was bad.

07:18.650 --> 07:23.040
Things are complicated between us, 
so it's kind of awkward,

07:23.040 --> 07:26.090
but you know what? 
She's a really nice girl. Really!

07:26.440 --> 07:30.170
So... you didn't believe 
those rumors were true?

07:30.170 --> 07:32.140
Huh? No.

07:32.140 --> 07:37.430
But actually, you don't really know, do you? 
What I was like before we dated.

07:37.430 --> 07:38.970
Well, no.

07:38.970 --> 07:44.010
But I like who you are now, Shirakawa-san.

07:45.280 --> 07:49.580
Also, I can tell when I look at you now

07:49.580 --> 07:52.220
that even in the past, 
you weren't the type of person to do that.

07:52.760 --> 07:53.950
Ryuto.

07:54.330 --> 07:57.930
So the past... it doesn't matter.

07:58.790 --> 08:00.660
The past is the past.

08:01.100 --> 08:02.630
The past is the past.

08:03.640 --> 08:06.010
Yeah! You're totally right!

08:06.010 --> 08:09.260
I won't stress about weird rumors and the past.

08:09.260 --> 08:11.130
Thanks, Ryuto!

08:12.120 --> 08:16.440
But I still wonder why Maria 
transferred to our school.

08:21.040 --> 08:24.650
What am I going to do? 
I can't believe I feel like this.

08:27.300 --> 08:31.830
No. I can't. I can't start to like him!

08:32.410 --> 08:36.940
If I fall for Kashima-kun, 
then I'll be second again!

08:40.550 --> 08:44.870
<i>The day after I announced at school 
that we're dating. And to be honest...</i>

08:44.870 --> 08:47.830
I don't wanna go!

08:49.900 --> 08:52.170
<i>They're all gonna point and laugh at me. 
Or they're gonna taunt me and say,</i>

08:52.570 --> 08:58.680
<i>"It'll take 500 million years before you're 
ready to date someone like Shirakawa-san!"</i>

08:59.050 --> 09:00.140
Good morning.

09:00.140 --> 09:02.890
Huh? Good... Good morning.

09:04.040 --> 09:06.600
<i>Everything's so normal, 
it's almost disappointing.</i>

09:07.520 --> 09:09.060
<i>But I guess that's right.</i>

09:09.060 --> 09:12.570
<i>News about who's dating who 
is only exciting for a second.</i>

09:12.570 --> 09:15.780
<i>Popular types have infinite 
other subjects to talk about.</i>

09:16.910 --> 09:19.000
Oh! Good morning, Ryuto.

09:19.370 --> 09:21.580
G-Good morning, Shirakawa-san!

09:24.790 --> 09:28.250
Yeah. It's like what you said to me before.

09:28.880 --> 09:32.230
You said you wanted to get 
into something that I liked, right?

09:32.920 --> 09:35.180
That made me so happy!

09:35.180 --> 09:39.320
So I want to get into something 
that you like too, Ryuto.

09:39.890 --> 09:44.570
<i>Shirakawa-san! I feel waves of 
adoration swelling up inside me!</i>

09:44.980 --> 09:47.260
What do you do on days you're free?

09:47.260 --> 09:50.650
N-Nothing I can really talk about.

09:50.650 --> 09:52.650
So you do something unspeakable?

09:52.650 --> 09:54.270
Th-That's not what I mean!

09:54.270 --> 09:56.220
I get it! You do dirty stuff!

09:56.220 --> 09:57.900
No, I don't!

09:58.220 --> 10:02.660
I, uh... like to watch live streams 
of games and stuff.

10:03.760 --> 10:06.280
Live streams? What's that?

10:06.280 --> 10:08.540
My favorite streamer is this guy named KEN.

10:08.540 --> 10:11.230
KEN is amazing because 
he's really good at all kinds of games!

10:11.230 --> 10:13.480
He started out as a pro gamer 
playing FPS games,

10:13.480 --> 10:16.300
but he's really good at crafting 
games and werewolf games too!

10:16.300 --> 10:19.580
But he doesn't rely on mainstream 
game theory and conventional strategies.

10:19.580 --> 10:22.120
Well, he does follow 
established rules, of course.

10:24.970 --> 10:27.680
<i>What the hell is wrong with me?!</i>

10:29.440 --> 10:32.160
I want to watch one of those live streams.

10:32.160 --> 10:34.400
Huh? O-Okay.

10:35.010 --> 10:36.120
Inside. Gotta gotta go in. Inside, inside.

10:35.360 --> 10:36.680
They're like this.

10:36.120 --> 10:38.460
<i>No way, not that way. Here, over here. Here.</i>

10:38.860 --> 10:42.450
Wow. So this KEN guy plays while he's talking?

10:42.450 --> 10:45.880
<i>Look right. I always check 
the right side once. On the right.</i>

10:45.490 --> 10:46.620
Whoa.

10:45.880 --> 10:48.320
<i>Good, good. All right. The right is clear.</i>

10:48.320 --> 10:51.290
<i>Okay, then in the back on the roof...</i>

10:49.070 --> 10:50.630
<i>Sh-She's close!</i>

10:52.420 --> 10:54.880
This game looks like fun!

10:55.310 --> 11:00.200
<i>If Shirakawa-san really is starting 
to like me more than before,</i>

11:00.990 --> 11:02.780
<i>then I want to do it!</i>

11:05.590 --> 11:07.140
Ah, indeed.

11:07.600 --> 11:12.590
Essentially, you want to kiss Shirakawa-san, 
but you don't know how.

11:12.590 --> 11:14.140
Do I have that right?

11:14.140 --> 11:15.640
Y-Yeah.

11:16.040 --> 11:17.690
Then, in that case,

11:18.440 --> 11:20.650
why the hell are you asking <i>us</i>?!

11:21.990 --> 11:24.760
Damn it! Damn it! 
Why does Kasshi get all the luck?

11:24.760 --> 11:27.070
Why don't you go and explode or something?!

11:27.070 --> 11:29.290
...is what I would like to say.

11:29.290 --> 11:32.710
But for friendship's sake, let's guide 
Kasshi on his path to manhood.

11:33.100 --> 11:35.670
You guys! Thanks!

11:35.960 --> 11:39.900
Well, when you train and sharpen your 
mind on the daily by gaming like we do,

11:39.900 --> 11:41.380
kissing strategy should pose no challenge.

11:43.390 --> 11:48.310
<b>Dead Jealous</b>

11:48.310 --> 11:52.690
Hey! Icchi! Nisshi! Hang in there, guys!

11:52.980 --> 11:55.810
You wouldn't have a chance! Are you kidding me?

11:56.090 --> 11:58.280
You're gonna make us piss blood from stress!

11:58.930 --> 12:02.810
That would be like trying to make 
champion with only white-level armor!

12:02.810 --> 12:05.210
My bad. I guess you're right.

12:05.210 --> 12:07.130
A kiss out of the blue...

12:07.700 --> 12:08.910
Hold on.

12:08.910 --> 12:10.830
If a kiss is too much, then what about

12:11.520 --> 12:13.850
trying to hold hands?

12:20.580 --> 12:22.380
Ueno Park?

12:22.380 --> 12:23.520
Uh, yeah.

12:23.520 --> 12:27.120
If it sounds good to you, I thought 
we could go there for our next date.

12:27.120 --> 12:28.380
Let's go!

12:28.850 --> 12:32.810
Ueno Park! I haven't gone since 
grade school! So many feels!

12:34.150 --> 12:37.260
And I get to go with you! I'm so stoked!

12:37.260 --> 12:39.970
All right. So next weekend, then.

12:39.970 --> 12:40.920
Yeah!

12:40.920 --> 12:43.150
<i>Yes! I cleared the first checkpoint!</i>

12:43.480 --> 12:47.120
<i>Actually, the three of us planned 
that out. Me, Isshi, and Nisshi.</i>

12:47.450 --> 12:50.580
<i>It's "Operation I Want to Hold 
Shirakawa-san's Hand."</i>

12:50.910 --> 12:55.370
<i>I'll invite her on a boat ride, real smooth, 
and when she tries to get in...</i>

12:57.760 --> 12:59.420
<i>The. Perfect. Plan.</i>

13:00.080 --> 13:02.800
So who's got the answer?

13:02.800 --> 13:03.760
Kashima-kun.

13:05.090 --> 13:07.390
<i>Oh crap! I wasn't listening!</i>

13:08.310 --> 13:10.380
Question 2 on page 32.

13:12.640 --> 13:14.980
Oh. Onomatopoeia.

13:15.440 --> 13:17.130
Yes, that is correct.

13:18.850 --> 13:20.440
Hey, thanks.

13:20.440 --> 13:25.110
Kashima-kun, I hope you don't start hating me.

13:27.510 --> 13:30.630
Don't worry. I don't hate you.

13:35.540 --> 13:39.500
<i>Wait, did I say something rude?</i>

13:47.990 --> 13:49.850
Wow!

13:53.970 --> 13:57.180
Oh, huh. I guess they have boats you can ride.

13:57.180 --> 13:59.650
Shirakawa-san, since we're here anyway...

13:59.650 --> 14:01.950
Um, actually, Ryuto...

14:01.950 --> 14:02.610
Hmm?

14:02.940 --> 14:06.200
I'm still not sure if I want to 
show you or not,

14:07.270 --> 14:09.820
but I brought something for you to eat.

14:10.480 --> 14:11.400
Huh?

14:11.400 --> 14:15.260
So just... here! I made you a bento!

14:15.620 --> 14:16.500
Huh?

14:17.040 --> 14:19.080
What?!

14:22.750 --> 14:26.250
Oh no! It's all messed up!

14:26.250 --> 14:28.710
No, it looks great!

14:28.710 --> 14:30.010
Thank you for the food!

14:35.990 --> 14:36.930
It's so good!

14:36.930 --> 14:40.020
Really? Yes!

14:42.850 --> 14:44.420
It's from Yamana-san.

14:44.980 --> 14:47.190
<b>Today</b>

14:44.980 --> 14:47.190
You finish the bento?
 If you leave any ur dead

14:48.150 --> 14:49.800
Typical Nicole!

14:49.800 --> 14:54.410
Actually, I made her call me over and over 
to wake me up so I'd have time to make it.

14:54.410 --> 14:59.090
<i>Dates with Shirakawa-san 
are so much fun. So, so much fun!</i>

14:59.090 --> 15:00.220
<i>But...</i>

15:01.360 --> 15:02.480
What's wrong?

15:02.950 --> 15:06.150
Nothing. This is just really good!

15:19.670 --> 15:21.690
It must feel good to ride those boats!

15:23.250 --> 15:24.400
Do you want to ride one?

15:25.350 --> 15:26.170
Yeah!

15:28.340 --> 15:29.820
Thank you very much.

15:30.250 --> 15:31.160
Go ahead.

15:31.160 --> 15:32.840
I'll get in first.

15:32.840 --> 15:34.740
Watch your step—

15:35.260 --> 15:36.320
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

15:42.930 --> 15:45.290
Hurry up and get in, Ryuto!

15:50.180 --> 15:52.170
Doesn't this feel great, Ryuto?

15:52.170 --> 15:52.840
Mm-hmm.

15:53.540 --> 15:57.310
<i>Just relax. I have one more 
chance when we get off.</i>

16:07.150 --> 16:09.500
The boat ride was so much fun.

16:09.500 --> 16:10.400
Yeah.

16:10.400 --> 16:12.280
What do you want to do next?

16:12.280 --> 16:13.530
I don't know.

16:13.530 --> 16:14.860
Go home?

16:14.860 --> 16:16.120
No...

16:16.680 --> 16:18.760
<i>I like her, so I want to touch her,</i>

16:18.760 --> 16:21.580
<i>but I like her, so I don't want to hurt her.</i>

16:24.080 --> 16:29.610
<i>If she knew what what I was thinking, 
I bet she'd put her own feelings aside</i>

16:29.610 --> 16:31.660
<i>and let me do whatever I want with her.</i>

16:32.340 --> 16:33.820
<i>But I can't do that.</i>

16:34.920 --> 16:37.610
<i>That would make me just like her exes!</i>

16:40.460 --> 16:43.860
Hey, Ryuto. If you have 
something to say, just say it.

16:44.940 --> 16:47.720
I know what that look means.

16:47.720 --> 16:52.650
We go on a normal date, and then they always 
start acting like that before they speak up.

16:52.650 --> 16:53.800
Huh?

16:54.320 --> 16:57.440
I seriously don't want to break up, though.

16:57.820 --> 17:00.700
W-Wait a second! What are you saying?

17:00.700 --> 17:03.000
Huh? You weren't about to break up with me?

17:03.000 --> 17:05.210
Huh?! No way!

17:05.210 --> 17:07.790
But you had a real serious look on your face!

17:07.790 --> 17:11.760
I have absolutely no intention of 
breaking up with you, Shirakawa-san!

17:12.120 --> 17:13.290
Really?

17:13.720 --> 17:18.380
I was just thinking that, um,

17:18.380 --> 17:21.320
I want to take one more boat ride.

17:21.320 --> 17:23.930
Huh? You like boats that much?

17:26.100 --> 17:30.360
Might as well, I guess. Let's go one more time!

17:31.800 --> 17:35.000
Yes! But this time let's ride a different one!

17:35.000 --> 17:35.700
Ah...

17:39.640 --> 17:41.860
<i>Change of course. My mind is made up.</i>

17:42.890 --> 17:44.860
<i>I'm done waiting.</i>

17:45.460 --> 17:48.420
<i>I just have to be brave and make my move.</i>

17:51.170 --> 17:52.130
Oh.

17:52.130 --> 17:55.020
Would you like... a hand?

17:58.660 --> 18:00.010
Thanks.

18:21.110 --> 18:24.830
Maybe we should've taken this boat first.

18:25.480 --> 18:27.790
Since I got to hold your hand.

18:27.790 --> 18:28.810
Huh?

18:29.750 --> 18:33.120
I've actually been thinking 
about that a lot recently.

18:33.120 --> 18:35.710
About how I want to hold your hand.

18:36.280 --> 18:40.930
So I've been trying to get a little closer 
to you. Haven't you noticed?

18:43.890 --> 18:48.810
M-Me too. I've been wanting 
to hold your hand too.

18:49.350 --> 18:50.900
For reals?

18:51.640 --> 18:52.810
For reals.

18:57.280 --> 18:59.720
Huh. Okay.

19:01.240 --> 19:03.200
Uh, Shirakawa-san?

19:15.560 --> 19:16.860
Gotcha.

19:16.860 --> 19:18.800
Shirakawa-san...

19:22.560 --> 19:25.960
We were both thinking the same thing, huh.

19:26.960 --> 19:34.230
You know, I want to get closer to you. 
I want to like you more. I want us...

19:35.320 --> 19:38.190
to really, truly care about each other.

19:47.840 --> 19:49.170
Here.

19:49.170 --> 19:50.380
Thank you.

19:52.540 --> 19:54.570
Shirakawa-san?

19:54.570 --> 19:57.340
Let's stay like this a little longer. Okay?

19:58.260 --> 19:59.340
Mm-hmm.

19:59.890 --> 20:03.930
But I mean, that "Shirakawa-san" thing? 
Can you drop that?

20:03.930 --> 20:04.800
Huh?

20:04.800 --> 20:07.510
My name is Runa, you know.

20:07.510 --> 20:10.960
<i>Calling a girl by her first name? 
And so casually?</i>

20:10.960 --> 20:13.730
<i>It's all happening so fast! 
My heart's not ready for this!</i>

20:15.040 --> 20:18.600
M'kay. Ru... Ru-Ru-Ru-Ru...

20:18.600 --> 20:19.930
Ruu-ru-ru-ru...

20:21.000 --> 20:21.950
Sorry.

20:22.240 --> 20:25.410
It's okay. I can wait until you get used to it.

20:30.870 --> 20:33.000
Your hand is cold, Ryuto.

20:33.000 --> 20:35.540
S-Sorry! It's because I'm so nervous.

20:35.540 --> 20:38.640
No problem. I'll warm it up for you.

20:38.640 --> 20:40.510
This is kind of embarrassing, though.

20:43.160 --> 20:46.970
It wouldn't have been this embarrassing 
if we had sex first, though.

20:47.670 --> 20:52.380
Holding hands, kissing... 
it's all so embarrassing now.

20:53.200 --> 20:58.150
But every time I feel you close to me, 
I think I fall for you a little more.

20:59.280 --> 21:01.860
<i>Shirakawa-san is here with me.</i>

21:02.170 --> 21:04.790
<i>I'll never let go of her hand!</i>

21:14.590 --> 21:16.000
I don't hate you.

21:17.320 --> 21:21.170
What am I supposed to do with these feelings?

21:23.950 --> 21:27.660
Someday, when you meet 
the person that you truly like,

21:27.660 --> 21:31.500
why don't you just aspire to be 
a person that he will love?

21:32.690 --> 21:38.150
A girl that Kashima-kun will love? 
Someone Kashima-kun will love?

21:39.050 --> 21:42.730
That's it. I'll just become Runa.

21:43.350 --> 21:45.180
I'll steal him from her.

21:51.090 --> 21:53.040
Just wait and see,

21:53.340 --> 21:54.440
Runa.

23:26.280 --> 23:27.960
On the next <i>Our Dating Story</i>,

23:27.960 --> 23:33.050
the inexperienced me 
spends the night with the experienced you.

23:33.540 --> 23:35.120
Spends the night?!

23:35.120 --> 23:38.060
What?! This is major!

23:38.060 --> 23:40.060
<b>Our Dating Story: The Inexperienced Me Spends the Night with the Experienced You</b>
